TIP:  "Trill" means to strum the bottom three strings of the (C) six times quickly.

TIP:  The ending of the instrumental bridge between verses is a little tricky.  To play the (D)(Dsus)(D) you simply hold the (D) and lift off the index finger (3rd string) while at the same time hammering your pinky on the the bottom string (3rd fret) and then reversing the process to get back to (D).  Like a pivot.  Practice it a few times.  If it's too uncomfortable then just lift off/replace the index finger and forget about the pinky, or play an (Em) in place of the (Dsus). 


